{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789389081,"nonce":"QNDLotmLqhmlSWTUb6h9da/7HnM=","message":"Done as a bytecode format rather than a snapshot layout change:\n`Format::Split` encodes the module's shell (globals, types, externs,\nand a stub per function with its id, name, signature and attributes\nand no blocks) plus each function body as its own postcard blob, with\nthe module's largest raw id. `deserialize_module_lazy` decodes the\nshell, relocating its ids by the next unminted id and advancing the\ncounter past the whole module; `LazyModule::function(id)` decodes a\nbody with the same base when the lowering adopts it\n(`adopt_prelowered_reached`). `deserialize_module` on a split file\nstill returns the whole module. The Python snapshot is written split.\n\nDecoding the builtins fell from 7.5 ms to about 1.5 for a program that\nreaches a hundred of the 425 functions; zypy's parse step from 9.5 ms\nto 3.5.","files":null}]}